-        <details class="faq"><summary>Does any Word document or long description become a benchmark?</summary><p>No. Use valid code/parameter sections or a versioned study JSON request. Unregistered algorithms require implementation.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Does a study run the production brain?</summary><p>A study runs reference algorithms on explicit inputs. Its report identifies mode=REFERENCE_STUDY and evidence type. Live outcome claims need suitable evidence.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>How do I repeat a study?</summary><p>Reuse the same request, data, seeds and implementation. A server dataset can change; retain the frozen resolved-request.json from evidence.zip.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Does /validate guarantee study success?</summary><p>It checks structure, limits and supplied trace shape. Server dataset availability and evidence completeness are checked at execution. PASS can later lead to NEEDS_DATA or PARTIAL.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Does /validate compile code or run Go tests?</summary><div><p>No. The /validate attachment caption checks file structure, options, parameter IDs and value domains, without queuing an experiment. Send the file with an empty caption to execute it. Go tests and replay preflight apply to code/parameter workflows. Studies use their own schema and evidence checks.</p></div></details>
+        <details class="faq"><summary>Does any Word document or long description become a benchmark?</summary><p>No. Use valid code/parameter sections, Cost/History study JSON, or declarative [endpoint] TXT/Markdown or endpoint JSON for the supported V2/V3 algorithm. Arbitrary edited prose remains a code request; new algorithms require implementation.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Does a study run the production brain?</summary><p>A study runs reference algorithms on explicit inputs. Its report identifies mode=REFERENCE_STUDY and evidence type. Live outcome claims need suitable evidence.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>How do I repeat a study?</summary><p>Reuse the same request, data, seeds and implementation. A server dataset can change; retain the frozen resolved-request.json from evidence.zip.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Does /validate guarantee study success?</summary><p>No. Syntax validity and read-only runtime readiness are separate results. Current stage identity, capture, matching ticks and endpoint history are checked before execution. Execution repeats identity/evidence checks and runs exact replay/tests. Cost/History reference studies still assess their own complete ledgers during execution; missing evidence can produce NEEDS_DATA or PARTIAL. READY is not a promise that a generated code change will pass.</p></details><details class="faq"><summary>Does /validate compile code or run Go tests?</summary><div><p>No. The /validate attachment caption checks syntax and separately reports live source/capture, matching snapshot count/freshness and required endpoint-history readiness without syncing snapshots/source, repinning, calling a model or queuing an experiment. Send the file with an empty caption to execute it. Go tests and replay preflight apply to code/parameter workflows. Studies use their own schema and evidence checks.</p></div></details>
         <details class="faq"><summary>Do bench and params in one file apply the values to the new code?</summary><div><p>Each section creates independent experiments with their own controls and reports, executed in file order. Parameter values are compared using the baseline replay binary. Testing a fixed candidate with parameter overrides requires a separate engineering workflow.</p></div></details>
         <details class="faq"><summary>Why does the activity bar not show a percentage?</summary><div><p>Model, test, build and replay durations are not known in advance. The card shows the actual stage and elapsed time with an activity indicator, refreshing every eight seconds while running. It records the terminal state when work finishes, fails, is cancelled or is interrupted by a restart.</p></div></details>
         <details class="faq" open><summary>Can I say “run the previous candidate again with 500 ticks”?</summary><div><p>Not through the current interface. Each /bench request is independent and the model regenerates a patch. Identical descriptions do not guarantee identical diffs. Compare the diff, baseline and data between runs. There is no /rerun command.</p></div></details>
